### =========================================================
### E-commerce (MiApp.WebApi) — http://localhost:7100
### Flujo completo. Ejecutá las requests en orden (PaymentService tiene que estar levantado).
### Las variables @token, @productId, etc. se completan solas con las respuestas anteriores.
### =========================================================

@shop = http://localhost:7100

### 1. Login del Admin (lo crea el seed al arrancar)
# @name loginAdmin
POST {{shop}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "admin@sistema.com", "password": "Admin123!" }

###
@adminToken = {{loginAdmin.response.body.token}}

### 2. Admin crea un producto barato (pago aprobado)
# @name prodBarato
POST {{shop}}/api/products
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "nombre": "Mouse", "descripcion": "Óptico", "precio": 15000, "stock": 10 }

### 3. Admin crea un producto caro (pago rechazado: supera 100000)
# @name prodCaro
POST {{shop}}/api/products
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "nombre": "Notebook", "descripcion": "i7", "precio": 900000, "stock": 5 }

###
@barato = {{prodBarato.response.body.id}}
@caro = {{prodCaro.response.body.id}}

### 4. Registrar un cliente (queda con rol Customer)
# @name register
POST {{shop}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Cliente", "email": "cliente@test.com", "password": "Cliente123!" }

### 5. Login del cliente
# @name loginCliente
POST {{shop}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "cliente@test.com", "password": "Cliente123!" }

###
@token = {{loginCliente.response.body.token}}
@clienteId = {{loginCliente.response.body.id}}

### 6. Listar productos (cualquier usuario logueado)
GET {{shop}}/api/products
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 7. Crear orden con el producto barato -> 201, estado Pending
# @name orden1
POST {{shop}}/api/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "items": [ { "productId": "{{barato}}", "quantity": 2 } ] }

###
@orden1 = {{orden1.response.body.id}}

### 8. Confirmar la orden -> el e-commerce llama a PaymentService -> Paid
POST {{shop}}/api/orders/{{orden1}}/confirm
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 9. Confirmar otra vez -> 400 (ya no está Pending)
POST {{shop}}/api/orders/{{orden1}}/confirm
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 10. Orden con el producto caro -> al confirmar queda PaymentRejected y vuelve el stock
# @name orden2
POST {{shop}}/api/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "items": [ { "productId": "{{caro}}", "quantity": 1 } ] }

###
POST {{shop}}/api/orders/{{orden2.response.body.id}}/confirm
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 11. Ver una orden (dueño o Admin)
GET {{shop}}/api/orders/{{orden1}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 12. Mis órdenes
GET {{shop}}/api/orders/my
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 13. Todas las órdenes con token de cliente -> 403 Forbidden
GET {{shop}}/api/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 14. Todas las órdenes con token de Admin -> 200
GET {{shop}}/api/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 15. Sin token -> 401 Unauthorized
GET {{shop}}/api/orders/my

### 16. Admin promueve al cliente a Admin (el cliente debe volver a loguearse)
PUT {{shop}}/api/users/{{clienteId}}/role
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "rol": "Admin" }

### CAMINO DE FALLO: apagá PaymentService, creá una orden y confirmala
### -> 503 Service Unavailable y la orden sigue Pending. Volvé a levantarlo y reintentá -> Paid.
